 "_doc": "uMgungundlovu DISTRICT Municipality (Pietermaritzburg, KZN) - Telkom /\nTFMC account [number removed] (old account [number removed]), Property Ref MPOF17441,\nMpofana_Book163_Seq30, Mooi River.  Municipal VAT reg 4000791642.\n\n*** THERE IS NO ELECTRICITY ON THESE BILLS. ***  This is a district\nmunicipality: it bills bulk WATER, SANITATION (sewer) and interest on\narrears only.  Across all 10 PDFs the strings \"electric\", \"kWh\" and \"kVA\"\noccur ZERO times.  The profile therefore has NO section:electricity rule and\nproduces NO electricity row - that is correct, not a miss.  Rows come out on\nwater / sewerage / sundry, and the \"canonical\" map (electricity only) is\nnever consulted.\n\nFINGERPRINT.  \"all\": the municipal VAT registration number 4000791642.\n\"any\": the masthead \"uMGUNGUNDLOVU DISTRICT MUNICIPALITY\", the remittance\nline \"uMgungundlovu District Municipality\" and the e-mail domain\numdm.gov.za.  NOTHING from the addressee block is used - not\n\"TFMC PTY LTD (Telkom)\", not \"PRIVATE BAG X137\", not \"CENTURION\", not\nTelkom's own VAT 4680101146 - and no CBRE/Excellerate address.  (Note\nuPhongolo's VAT 4000791873 shares a prefix with ours but is a different\nnumber; substring matching keeps them apart.)\n\nFILENAME vs BILL.  UMG_[number removed]_Accounts Receivable Statements\n[number removed].pdf has 7447 in its NAME but its text reads\n\"Account No. [number removed]\" - the same account.  The app reads the account\nnumber out of the bill text, never the filename, so it is handled as one\naccount.  It is the May-2026 statement (Period Ending 2026/05/31), and its\nreadings 9360 -> 9452 chain exactly between the April charges (in the\nMay shape-C bill) and the June charges (in the July shape-C bill).\n\nTHREE TEMPLATES (established from --raw before any pattern was written):\n\n  Shape A - 6 bills, \"Statement_<acct>_<date>.pdf\", Sep 2025 - Jan 2026\n    (2026-01-31 is present TWICE, byte-identical apart from the filename).\n    Ledger columns  Date | Description | Reference | Vat | Amount (Inc Vat) |\n    Balance.  Consumption line reads \"71 KL (Start:9023 End:9094)\" and is\n    followed by sub-lines \"Meter:KZ223_PM[number removed]  Reading Date: ...\n    Reading Type: Actual Reading\", \"Previous Reading: ... End Reading: ...\n    Consumption:71\", and a \"Band: 0 - 71 = 71 Kl @ R83.60 = R5 935.60\" line\n    that prints the ex-VAT amount INDEPENDENTLY.  Group headings Other /\n    Water Consumption / Water Basic / Sanitation are printed.\n    MONEY IS PERIOD-DECIMAL (\"6 825.94\" or \"4,326.30\") - safe to capture\n    whole.\n\n  Shape B - 1 bill, \"Accounts Receivable Statements [number removed].pdf\",\n    May 2026.  Same columns as shape A, but the descriptions are one-liners\n    (\"Water Consumption 92KL - [9360 to 9452]\", \"Sanitation Household 92KL -\n    [9360 to 945\" - truncated by the column width) and there are NO meter\n    sub-lines and NO Band lines.  Money is period-decimal.\n\n  Shape C - 3 bills, \"[number removed]*.pdf\", statements Mar / May / Jul 2026.\n    Different masthead (\"uMGUNGUNDLOVU DISTRICT MUNICIPALITY\" at the top),\n    ledger columns  Date | Description | DEBIT | VAT | Credit | Balance -\n    i.e. the inc-VAT amount comes BEFORE the VAT, the opposite order to\n    shapes A/B - and dates are dd/mm/yyyy.  Each charge is followed by a\n    meter table whose \"Exclusive\" column prints the ex-VAT amount\n    INDEPENDENTLY.  MONEY IS COMMA-DECIMAL / SPACE-THOUSANDS (\"5 864,54\").\n    Its \"Period Ending\" is the statement month while the ledger lines carry\n    the PREVIOUS month's charges.\n\nBECAUSE THE COLUMN ORDER FLIPS between shapes, the VAT/inc pairs cannot\nshare one rule with \"patterns\" fallbacks (rule: every alternative must\nexpose the same groups in the same order).  Each charge type therefore has\nTWO rules - *_ab (Vat then Amount) and *_c (Debit then VAT) - merged by\n'prefer' computes.\n\nMONEY IS VAT-INCLUSIVE on every shape, with the VAT printed in its own\ncolumn, so every ex-VAT figure is derived per line with a 'sub' compute and\nthen cross-checked against the independently printed Band (shape A) /\nExclusive (shape C) amount.  water_usage_r and sewer_r PREFER the printed\nfigure and fall back to inc-minus-VAT (shape B, which prints neither).\n\nCOMMA DECIMALS (shape C only).  _to_decimal() strips spaces AND commas, so a\nfull capture of \"5 864,54\" would arrive as 586454 - 100x too big.  Following\nthe Ditsobotla convention the shape-C money patterns capture the RAND PART\nONLY, so those 3 bills read up to R0.99 low per figure, and the exact\nprinted string is kept in umg_*_txt natives.  Shapes A/B (7 of 10 bills) are\ncent-exact.  The two-line engine fix is in reports/ditsobotla.md sec 2.\n\nSECTIONS.  Shape C prints NO group headings at all, and on the Dec-2025\nshape-A bill the \"Sanitation\" heading sits above the INTEREST line, above\nthe water rows.  So the only reliable boundary is the ledger header\n(\"Date  Description ...\"), which exists on all three shapes: water is the\nsingle boundary-forming section (ledger header -> end of document) and\nsewerage / sundry are overlays with \"end\": \"\\\\Z\".  Every rule anchors on its\nown description text, which is unique per service (\"Water Consumption\" /\n\"<n> KL (Start:\" / \"Water Basic\" / \"SEWER VARIABLE\" / \"Sanitation Household\"\n/ \"Interest Charge\"), so nothing can leak between services.  The two \"last\nBand / last Exclusive\" sewer rules use a greedy [\\\\s\\\\S]* prefix precisely\nbecause the overlay can begin above the water rows.\n\nPAYMENTS.  \"Direct Deposit - Water\" credits are reported in \"recon\"\n(incoming_payment), not as a charge row.  On shape C the credit sits in the\nCredit column (third money on the line), on shapes A/B it is a negative in\nthe Amount column.\n\nFIELD NAMES follow Data/views/general.view.json so the General view renders\nthem: water -> w_meter, w_reading_type, w_read_start, w_read_end,\nstart_reading_kl, end_reading_kl, total_kl, water_usage_r, water_levy_r,\nwater_charges_r; sewerage -> sewer_kl, sewer_r, ws_vat_r, ws_total_ex_r,\nws_total_r; sundry -> sundry_charges_r, sundry_vat_r, sundry_total_ex_r,\nsundry_total_r; plus site_name / statement_month / account_number.\n\nKNOWN LIMITS (see reports/umgungundlovu.md):\n  - shape C wraps the meter id over two lines (\"KZ223_PM14\" + \"[number removed]\"), so\n    w_meter reads \"KZ223_PM14 [number removed]\" there against \"KZ223_PM[number removed]\" on\n    shape A.  Nothing else can rejoin them - 'concat' inserts a space.\n  - shape A prints one Reading Date, not a reading period, so\n    w_read_start/w_read_end fill only on the 3 shape-C bills.\n  - the Nov-2025 shape-A bill prints no Band lines and no\n    Previous/End Reading values under Sanitation, so its water ex-VAT falls\n    back to inc-minus-VAT.\n  - no bill prints an independent water+sewer ex-VAT TOTAL, so\n    water_charges_r is the sum of its own parts; the genuine checks are the\n    printed Band/Exclusive figures and the printed per-line VAT.",
